<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav November industry output falls 7.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav November industry output falls 7.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT  NOV 96	OCT 96     OCT 95</p>
<p> pct change mth/mth	    -  7.2	 + 15.4	n.a.</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr		+ 14.4	 + 12.6	n.a.</p>
<p> index (base average 1995)    118.4	  126.9	n.a.</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE DATA (JAN TO NOV)</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr		+  7.3	 +  6.7	n.a.</p>
<p>SEASONALLY ADJUSTED DATA</p>
<p> index (base average 1995)    113.8	  110.4	n.a.</p>
<p>NOTES - Industrial output in November 1996 was 37.7 percent down against the same month in 1991.</p>
<p>Cumulative January-November 1996 industry output was 44.8 percent below the same eleven-month period in 1991.</p>
<p>Data largely exclude private sector, where manufacturing is not significant.</p>
<p>-- Amra kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 2224305</p>
